  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Plage Beau Rivage is a private beach with a lounge bar, 253 sunbeds and a restaurant open all year, at 107 quai des États-Unis in Nice, opposite the Hôtel Beau Rivage. The official website places it along the Promenade des Anglais; the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office describes it as "one beach, two atmospheres: zen and trendy". The restaurant (450 covers) serves Mediterranean cuisine made in-house from fresh, local produce. The establishment holds the Clef Verte and Qualité Tourisme labels.</p>
      <h2>Dogs: conflicting sources</h2>
      <p>The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office pages (restaurant and beach), repeated by Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme, state that "pets are not accepted". On the other hand, the operator's page, Hôtels 3A La Collection, lists a "Pet friendly label" among the beach's services, whereas the Nice pet friendly label was first awarded to the Hôtel Beau Rivage. With no clear rule, don't count on your dog being welcome without the establishment's prior agreement.</p>
      <h2>Practical information</h2>
      <p>The phone number given by the official website is 04 92 00 46 80. According to the tourist office, the restaurant serves lunch all year (12pm-3pm off-season); from 15 May to 19 September, it is open from 12pm to 4pm and from 7pm to 10:30pm, and the lounge from 10am to midnight. No car park belongs to the establishment: the website points to nearby paid car parks (Sulzer and cours Saleya). Wheelchair access is possible with assistance.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call 04 92 00 46 80 before coming with your dog, since the official sources disagree.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Promenade des Anglais is perfect for a long walk before or after your meal, and Old Nice is very close.</p>
